  "verdict": "parity",
  "finding": "Auth carrier on the wire: genai used x-goog-api-key-header, the AI SDK used x-goog-api-key-header (same form). Custom header reached the wire: genai=true, ai-sdk=true; its VALUE matched what was sent (expected \"p01\"): genai=true, ai-sdk=true. llxprt User-Agent survived: genai=true, ai-sdk=true; the value carries the LLxprt-Code prefix: genai=true, ai-sdk=true (sent UA: genai \"LLxprt-Code/probe-2761 (darwin; arm64)\", ai-sdk \"LLxprt-Code/probe-2761 (darwin; arm64) ai-sdk/google/2.0.85 ai-sdk/provider-utils/3.0.30 runtime/bun/1.3.14\"). A deliberately invalid key produced genai=rejected and ai-sdk=rejected (rejection requires an auth-shaped status or an API_KEY_INVALID payload; a transient status is inconclusive). The header stamping and custom-header merge in GeminiProvider.createHttpOptions carries over unchanged, values included."
